{
  // THE TOOLS SWEEP – R2-12 / TOK-09. `npm run check:tools`.
  //
  // ⚠ NOT REFERENCED FROM `tsconfig.json`, AND THAT IS THE POINT. `vue-tsc -b` builds the projects
  // the root config references; this one is deliberately outside that graph, so the 151 archival
  // probes in `tools/` stop being typechecked on every `npm run build`. The 26 live instruments are
  // listed in `tsconfig.app.json` and still are.
  //
  // WHAT IT IS FOR. An archival probe is evidence – the reproduction that settled an argument – and
  // evidence that no longer compiles is evidence you cannot re-run.
  //
  // ⭐⭐ AND SINCE ROUND 34 IT IS NOT "ON DEMAND" ANY MORE: `npm run check` runs it, and so does CI
  // (QA-34 of the 02.09 principles review). «On demand» meant «by whoever remembers», and the
  // measurement of what that was worth is nine TypeScript errors across six tools sitting unread
  // for months – two of them, both `r29-item14-*`, wrong on the day they were written, so those
  // probes printed `undefined` and `NaN` into their own evidence and no run ever objected. Two
  // earlier waves saw the redness, wrote it down as «baseline», and moved on, which is what a check
  // nobody runs is actually for.
  //
  // ⚠ THE COST WAS MEASURED BEFORE IT WAS WIRED IN, because the review offered a scheduled job as
  // the escape hatch if it were expensive: 2.49 / 2.49 / 2.56 s over three runs on this Mac, beside
  // 6.81 s for the `vue-tsc -b --force` already in the gate and minutes for the unit suite after
  // it. At ~2.5 s it does not need an escape hatch, so it takes the every-PR slot the review
  // preferred. It is placed AFTER `vue-tsc -b --force`: the app's own errors should be the first
  // thing a reader sees, and the tools cannot be right while the engine they import is wrong.
  //
  // ⚠ `composite: false` on purpose. A composite project would want emit and a build-info file, and
  // this project never emits anything; it exists to be typechecked and thrown away.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "composite": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "tsBuildInfoFile": null
  },
  "include": ["tools/**/*.ts"]
}
